<meta type=article>
  <title | Inline Formatting Sweep>
</meta>

<section | Semantic versus visual inline>
The two semantic inline elements are
<!-- cell: em/form:pipe -->
<em | emphasis> and
<!-- cell: strong/form:pipe -->
<strong | strong importance>. Their visual-only cousins, reached only by writing
the tag explicitly, are
<!-- cell: b/blanket -->
<b | bold>,
<!-- cell: i/blanket -->
<i | italic>,
<!-- cell: u/blanket -->
<u | underline>, and
<!-- cell: s/blanket -->
<s | struck through>.

<!-- cell: em/form:long -->
The same-line long form also works: <em>emphasised</em> and <strong>important</strong>.

<section | The rest of the inline set>
Monospaced
<!-- cell: code/blanket -->
<code | render()> code, a
<!-- cell: span/blanket -->
<span | styled span>, a
<!-- cell: q/blanket -->
<q | short quotation>, an
<!-- cell: abbr/blanket -->
<abbr title="HyperText Markup Language" | HTML> abbreviation, a
<!-- cell: kbd/blanket -->
<kbd | Ctrl+C> keystroke, a
<!-- cell: var/blanket -->
<var | x> variable, a
<!-- cell: samp/blanket -->
<samp | sample output> sample, and an
<!-- cell: output/blanket -->
<output | 42> result.

Water is written H
<!-- cell: sub/blanket -->
<sub | 2>O, and the area scales as r
<!-- cell: sup/blanket -->
<sup | 2>. The same is reachable with the TeX shortcuts H_{2}O and x^{2}, which
lower to sub/sup respectively.
